  "response_text": "Our stack allocation method divides the stack memory into two sections, one for the main stack of a certain size and the other for thread specific stacks, each of the same size. The main stack contains setup, interrupts, and other OS-specific memory, whereas the thread stacks will have memory which is used when running different threads. We got the new value for PSP_val by subtracting 0x400 from MSP_init_val, and so we needed to know the initial location of MSP to do so. You would not want to set PSP_val to the address of a random memory location, and so it is better to set it a certain distance from MSP_init_val.\\n",
